index 9d1cd17..c9bb05a 100644
--- a/docs/change_log/release-3.4.md
+++ b/docs/change_log/release-3.4.md
@@ -58,6 +58,24 @@ In addition, the `md_globals` parameter of
 `Markdown.extensions.Extension.extendMarkdown()` is no longer recognized as a
 valid parameter and will raise an error if provided.
 
+### Backslash unescaping moved to Treeprocessor
+
+Unescaping backslash escapes has been moved to a Treeprocessor, which runs
+before the document is serialized. Previously, a Postprocessor unescaped them
+after serialization, which meant that an escaped character which needs to be
+escaped in HTML (such as `\"` with the [smarty] extension enabled, or `\>`)
+was output unescaped, possibly resulting in invalid HTML. For example,
+`![x\"x](x)` would render as `<img alt="x"x" src="x" />`.
+
+The new `markdown.treeprocessors.UnescapeTreeprocessor` is registered as
+`unescape` with a priority of `0`. The `unescape` Postprocessor has been
+removed from the default Postprocessors and
+`markdown.postprocessors.UnescapePostprocessor` is now deprecated and will be
+removed in a future release. Any extension which relied on the `unescape`
+Postprocessor should be updated to use the Treeprocessor.
+
+[smarty]: ../extensions/smarty.md
+
 ## New features
 
 The following new features have been included in the 3.4 release:
@@ -97,3 +115,5 @@ The following bug fixes are included in the 3.4 release:
 
 * Extension entry-points are only loaded if needed (#1216).
 * Added additional checks to the `<pre><code>` handling of `PrettifyTreeprocessor` (#1261, #1263).
+* Unescape backslash escapes before serializing so that characters such as `"`
+  are properly escaped in attribute values.
